{
  "case": "count active users",
  "variant": "with",
  "trial": 0,
  "run": {
    "final_text": "I wrote `report.py` and ran it. It prints:\n\n```\nactive users: 3\n```\n\nThe `acme-client-guide` skill is out of date, and following it gave the wrong answer at first. It says a user is active when `state == \"enabled\"`, which counted all 5 users. But the `acme_client.py` in this folder is version 2.0. Its docstring says `state` is kept only for backwards compatibility, is always `\"enabled\"`, and shouldn't be used. Version 2.0 uses an `active` true/false field instead, so the script now counts users where `u[\"active\"]` is true. That's 3 of the 5.\n\nThe skill is also wrong about `created_at`. In 2.0 it's in seconds, not milliseconds, so dividing by 1000 as the skill says would give wrong dates. `report.py` doesn't use dates, so this doesn't affect it. You should update `.claude/skills/acme-client-guide/SKILL.md` so the next script doesn't get these wrong.",
